py-flowtoken is an independent Python adaptation of FlowToken by Ephibbs
and contributors: https://github.com/Ephibbs/flowtoken

The named animation effects and their keyframe definitions are adapted from
FlowToken. The README demonstration GIF comes from the original FlowToken
README: https://nextjs-omega-five-46.vercel.app/demo.gif

Python rendering, framework adapters, streaming state, and the browser
renderer are implemented in this repository. No upstream React runtime is
included in the distribution. py-flowtoken is released under the MIT License
in LICENSE.
